.claude/
.venv/
__pycache__/
_build/
# what the upstream fetchers download, in this repository and in every cut of it. The fetchers
# create it themselves, so no cut ships the directory to hold it.
sources/
# solved model problems, keyed on the solver's source and inputs, written by the paper that solves.
# NO trailing slash: a release may put a SYMLINK at this path, and a pattern ending in "/"
# matches a directory alone, so the slash let the link itself be committed into the published
# repository, where it pointed at a path only one machine has (measured 2026-09-18).
code/.cache
# working files the clean-room implementation regenerates (see its README)
code/cleanroom/csv*/
code/cleanroom/paper.txt
# generated by code/theme.py from the econ-ark-myst submodule plus content/theme/local.css
content/theme/site.css
# What a typst SOURCE export writes beside the .typ. The first six are copies of the theme's
# own files (the theme split into ark/ and brand/ on 2026-09-22), so tracking them would state
# the theme twice; the rest MyST regenerates from the page and the bibliography on every build.
content/exports/econark.typ
content/exports/econ-ark.typ
content/exports/ark/
content/exports/brand/
content/exports/ark-subpar.typ
content/exports/logo.png
content/exports/myst-imports.typ
content/exports/main.bib
content/exports/files/
# Each page's typst source. It references content/exports/files/*.png, which are not tracked,
# so it cannot compile as shipped, and MyST names those files from the BUILD DIRECTORY rather
# than their bytes, so every cut rewrote three of its lines for no content change (2026-09-18).
# A glob, since this file ships in every cut and a per-page line would name private pages.
content/exports/*.typ